{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-10038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}z+2y+7x=1 \\\\ 3y-z=-2 \\\\ 4y-2z-3x=0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-10038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}7x+2y+z=1 \\\\ 3y-z=-2 \\\\ -3x+4y-2z=0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =7|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =7(-6+4)-2(-3)+1(9) \\\\  & =-14+6+9 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 9 \\\\ -8 & -11 & 34 \\\\ -5 & -7 & 21\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 8 & -11 & -34 \\\\ -5 & 7 & 21\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -11 & 7 \\\\ 9 & -34 & 21\\text{ }\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -11 & 7 \\\\ 9 & -34 & 21\\text{ }\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -11 & 7 \\\\ 9 & -34 & 21\\text{ }\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 25 \\\\ 77\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=-18,\\,y=25,\\,z=77.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-10038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f4019fdcf8654eed629fb977bd057ce9511930e87324ac8b8d3a8f9f7a842c67"} {"question" "q-10038" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-10038" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-11,\\,y=19,\\,z=77"] ["math" "x=-13,\\,y=19,\\,z=57"] ["math" "x=-18,\\,y=25,\\,z=77"] ["math" "x=13,\\,y=19,\\,z=77"] ["math" "x=13,\\,y=25,\\,z=77"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-10038" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=-18,\\,y=25,\\,z=77"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-10075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3z-y+x-5=0 \\\\ y+2x+2z=1 \\\\ z-2x-2y=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-10075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x-y+3z=5 \\\\ 2x+y+2z=1 \\\\ -2x-2y+z=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(1+4)+1(2+4)+3(-4+2) \\\\  & =5+6-6 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 7 & -4 \\\\ -5 & -4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -6 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -5 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -5 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -5 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -\\frac{19}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=3,y=-\\frac{19}{5},z=-\\frac{3}{5}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-10075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f4019fdcf8654eed629fb977bd057ce9511930e87324ac8b8d3a8f9f7a842c67"} {"question" "q-10075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-10075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-3,y=-\\frac{19}{5},z=-\\frac{3}{5}"] ["math" "x=15,y=-19,z=-3"] ["math" "x=15,y=19,z=-3"] ["math" "x=3,y=-\\frac{19}{5},z=-\\frac{3}{5}"] ["math" "x=3,y=\\frac{19}{5},z=\\frac{3}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-10075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=3,y=-\\frac{19}{5},z=-\\frac{3}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-10101" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x-z=0 \\\\ x+y+3z=2 \\\\ 3x-2y+z=4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-10101" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(1-3(-2))+0-1(-2-3) \\\\  & =1+6+2+3 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -8 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=\\frac{2}{3},y=-\\frac{2}{3},z=\\frac{2}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-10101" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f4019fdcf8654eed629fb977bd057ce9511930e87324ac8b8d3a8f9f7a842c67"} {"question" "q-10101" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-10101" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-\\frac{2}{3},y=-\\frac{2}{3},z=-\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "x=8,y=-8,z=8"] ["math" "x=8,y=8,z=8"] ["math" "x=\\frac{2}{3},y=-\\frac{2}{3},z=\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "x=\\frac{2}{3},y=\\frac{2}{3},z=\\frac{2}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-10101" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\frac{2}{3},y=-\\frac{2}{3},z=\\frac{2}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-78567" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a matrix equation ${A}^{-1}B\\,x=d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $6\\times 6$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $6\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-78567" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Pre-multiplying both sides of the equation ${A}^{-1}B\\,x=d$ by $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}B\\,x & =d \\\\ A{A}^{-1}B\\,x & =A\\,d \\\\ {I}_{6}B\\,x & =A\\,d \\\\ B\\,x & =A\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $B$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${B}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $B\\,x=A\\,d$ by ${B}^{-1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B\\,x & =A\\,d \\\\ {B}^{-1}B\\,x & ={B}^{-1}A\\,d \\\\ {I}_{6}\\,x & ={B}^{-1}A\\,d \\\\ x & ={B}^{-1}A\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-78567" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f4019fdcf8654eed629fb977bd057ce9511930e87324ac8b8d3a8f9f7a842c67"} {"question" "q-78567" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-78567" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=A\\,d\\,{B}^{-1}"] ["math" "x=A{B}^{-1}\\,d"] ["math" "x=BA\\,d"] ["math" "x={B}^{-1}A\\,d"] ["math" "x={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-78567" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x={B}^{-1}A\\,d"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-78569" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a matrix equation ${B}^{-1}\\,x=A\\,d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $9\\times 9$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $9\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-78569" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Pre-multiplying both sides of the equation ${B}^{-1}\\,x=A\\,d$ by $B,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{-1}\\,x & =A\\,d \\\\ B{B}^{-1}\\,x & =BA\\,d \\\\ {I}_{9}\\,x & =BA\\,d \\\\ x & =BA\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-78569" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f4019fdcf8654eed629fb977bd057ce9511930e87324ac8b8d3a8f9f7a842c67"} {"question" "q-78569" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-78569" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=AB\\,d"] ["math" "x=A\\,d\\,B"] ["math" "x=A\\,d{B}^{-1}"] ["math" "x=BA\\,d"] ["math" "x={B}^{-1}A\\,d"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"} {"question" "q-78569" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=BA\\,d"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067981/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e144f458d183b98a5efc50b1787a8560bee1d14f877e3c0525d2325a72c3318"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2272 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
